  "headline": "Indonesian Parliament Sets December Deadline For New Vice President",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Prepares To Elect New Vice President",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian parliament has scheduled the election of a new vice president for December 2 after receiving nominations from President Prabowo Subianto.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The People's Consultative Assembly of Indonesia has scheduled the plenary session to elect a new vice president for December 2, 2026.",
    "President Prabowo Subianto is expected to submit two candidate names by November 18, with nominees not restricted to the current coalition.",
    "A 36-member verification and ad hoc committee has been established by the parliament to oversee the selection process."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the resignation of former Vice President Gibran, the Indonesian People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has initiated the formal procedure to select a replacement. The assembly has formed a 36-person verification and ad hoc team to manage the election process. MPR Speaker Ahmad Muzani announced that the parliament will officially request two candidate names from President Prabowo Subianto, with a submission deadline set for November 18, 2026. The assembly clarified that nominees do not strictly have to originate from the ruling political coalition. President Prabowo is reportedly planning to consult with coalition party leaders regarding the selection. The constitutional authority to propose these candidates lies solely with the president. The process is expected to culminate in a plenary session on December 2, 2026, where the new vice president will be elected to fill the existing vacancy in the national administration.",
